    body = "When multiple agents run in parallel, they inevitably need to record decisions or learnings. Writing to the same file creates race conditions and merge conflicts. The drop-box pattern solves this cleanly: each agent writes to its own file (e.g., decisions/inbox/agent-name-slug.md), and a Scribe agent merges them into the canonical shared file afterward. Simple idea, dramatic improvement in parallel throughput. We went from serializing agents 'because of shared state' to full fan-out overnight."
